## Mission

Build a programme-level theory and empirical study of **scientific failure as epistemic structure**.

The target is much broader than “store negative results” or “reflect on failed trajectories.” Ask:

> When a scientific claim, experiment, theory, method, representation, Jump attempt, or research programme fails, what exactly has been learned, what future possibilities should be removed or downweighted, what possibilities should be newly opened, and how can that knowledge transfer without becoming stale or overgeneralized?

A future ORION should become better not only by accumulating successful mechanics, but by accumulating **scoped negative knowledge, failed transformation traces, and explanations of why promising routes did not work**.

