## Recurrence and stale negative knowledge

A central problem is **negative transfer**.

A prior failure `f` should affect a new episode only if a compatibility relation holds:

```text
Compatible(f, R_new, C_new, assumptions_new) = true
```

Pressure dimensions such as:

- same method/operator class;
- same load-bearing assumptions;
- same representation regime;
- same measurement/interface;
- same target/function;
- same authority/evaluator semantics.

A regime change may reopen previously failed routes. Failure memory therefore requires staleness/expiry/revalidation, not permanent prohibition.

## Information value of failure

Do not equate failure value with one entropy number. Pressure several effects separately:

- hypotheses/causes eliminated;
- search branches pruned;
- new revision class opened;
