## Bounded reachability criterion

For target family `C` and registered resource/complexity bound `B`, pressure whether:

```text
C ∉ Reach_B(R)
```

but

```text
C ∈ Reach_B(R ⊕ concept)
```

or whether the new representation reduces derivational/construction cost enough to cross the registered bound.

Raw logical expressivity increase is **not required**: conservative re-representations may count if they change bounded reachability and survive no-Jump controls.

## Positive families

Use invented worlds where the hidden solution requires one of several structural changes but exact symbol names are randomized:

- latent-object invention required for intervention transfer;
- quotient/identification reveals a hidden invariant;
- split/contextualization resolves contradictory local laws;
- representation lift makes a stable mechanism local/simple;
- coordinate/frame change exposes symmetry and a protected consequence;
- bridge primitive unifies two exact local theories;
- causal refactor enables protected interventions;
- new affordance/function primitive enables a useful design absent from the current task ontology.

