## Recursive decomposition study

After a broad concept-invention positive, test transformation families factorially or in matched families.

Possible outcomes:

- one general `REPRESENTATION_TRANSFORM` parent explains all;
- several independent atoms survive (`INTRODUCE`, `SPLIT`, `QUOTIENT`, `LIFT`, etc.);
- cross-domain analogy is the actual load-bearing parent and concept invention adds no value;
- concept generation matters only with thought-experiment evidence (#511 interaction-only);
- executable semantics/correspondence, not proposal generation, is the true bottleneck.

Do not retain a grand “concept invention” module if the effect localizes to standard representation-learning/abstraction mechanisms.

